Bootstrap workspace

cd bootstrap
terraform init
terraform apply -auto-approve
→ Creates S3/DynamoDB or GCS bucket tracked by Terraform.



Main workspace

cd ../main
terraform init -reconfigure
terraform apply
→ Migrates state into the remote backend provisioned by bootstrap.

This pattern ensures:

Backend infra is tracked by Terraform (not just CLI).

You can destroy/recreate backend cleanly if needed.

Separation of concerns: bootstrap manages state infra, main manages workloads.

